d Gandalf + researchPrime commission-envelope EMITTERS; the no-inline-reimplementation boundary canary (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n90\t**Depends on:** Coverage-stamp canary\n91\t**done-when:** envelopes emit (never dispatch) and the boundary canary fails the build on an inline reimplementation.\n92\t- **Given** an inline researchPrime/Gandalf reimplementation, **when** the boundary canary runs, **then** the build fails (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n93\t\n94\t## Wave 14 â€” M1 read-only dispatch shim (B-shim) â€” closes Milestone M1 (comprehension-only preview)\n95\t**Deliverables:** a minimal read-only single-pillar dispatch shim.\n96\t**Depends on:** Commission emitters + no-inline boundary canary\n97\t**done-when:** the shim routes a user request to UNDERSTAND read-only and satisfies the EXACT predicate the Wave-23 no-dispatch canary will later assert: **no commission-id emitted AND no rung-flip on any shim path** (wave-local check; regression-bound by Wave 23).\n98\t- **Given** any shim path, **when** Wave-14's check runs, **then** no commission-id is emitted and no rung is flipped.\n99\t\n100\t## Wave 15 â€” Generation + typed-claim decompose (C1)\n101\t**Deliverables:** a stateless Polya/Schoenfeld GENERATION pass â†’ typed-claim DECOMPOSE into the A1 ledger.\n102\t**Depends on:** M1 read-only dispatch shim\n103\t**done-when:** a new problem yields a candidate decomposed into typed claims, all at UNVERIFIED, in the ledger.\n104\t- **Given** a new problem, **when** C1 runs, **then** every emitted claim is at UNVERIFIED until the router verifies it.\n105\t\n106\t## Wave 16 â€” Claim-type dispatch classifier (C2)\n107\t**Deliverables:** a fail-safe, separate-pass claim-type DISPATCH classifier with conservative escalation to the proof route.\n108\t**Depends on:** Generation + typed-claim decompose\n109\t**done-when:** ambiguous/borderline claims escalate conservatively to the proof route (ABSTAIN+route), never silently to autonomous-VERIFIED (tested).\n110\t- **Given** a borderline claim, **when** C2 runs, **then** it routes to the proof route (ABSTAIN), never to autonomous-VERIFIED.\n111\t\n112\t## Wave 17 â€” Metacognitive CONTROL state machine + ABANDON fixture (C3)\n113\t**Deliverables:** the CONTROL state machine; the S1 thresholds + gap-function (budget=8; switch=no progress in last 3; ABANDON=2 consecutive switches); graded over a pinned progress-boolean stream.\n114\t**Depends on:** Claim-type dispatch classifier\n115\t**done-when:** on the pinned canned non-converging fixture the machine ABANDONs via the GAP-FUNCTION strictly before step 8 (reason=gap-function, not budget-exhausted), leaving the claim UNVERIFIED/CONJECTURAL.\n116\t- **Given** the pinned non-converging fixture, **when** CONTROL runs, **then** it ABANDONs with reason=gap-function before step 8.\n117\t\n118\t## Wave 18 â€” In-process adversarial advisory layer (C4)\n119\t**Deliverables:** the in-process Gandalf/researchPrime critique + faithfulness-restatement discipline, writing the NOTES field ONLY.\n120\t**Depends on:** Metacognitive CONTROL state machine + ABANDON fixture\n121\t**done-when:** advisory critique writes NOTES and can never change a rung (tested).\n122\t- **Given** an advisory critique, **when** C4 runs, **then** the NOTES field updates but the rung is unchanged.\n123\t\n124\t## Wave 19 â€” DIALOGUE state machine (D1)\n125\t**Deliverables:** the Lakatos loop; mixed-initiative; the structured emission contract; Grice Quality + the degradation contract (CONJECTURAL + advisory payload + \"promote Phase F\" affordance); the anti-sycophancy sticky ledger; a D1 abstain fixture.\n126\t**Depends on:** In-process adversarial advisory layer\n127\t**done-when:** dialogue asserts-as-settled ONLY VERIFIED claims; every ABSTAIN carries an advisory payload.\n128\t- **Given** an unverified proof claim, **when** the user asks \"is this settled?\", **then** the agent answers CONJECTURAL + advisory payload, never settled.\n129\t\n130\t## Wave 20 â€” FORMALIZE Lakatosian loop (D2)\n131\t**Deliverables:** the definition-forging loop; the P3 example-space-stability predicate (ADVISORY-only); the example/monster regression suite; the autonomous emitter/abstain stub (formalize_status:requires-Phase-F); a D2 abstain fixture.\n132\t**Depends on:** DIALOGUE state machine\n133\t**done-when:** autonomous D2 never emits green; a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F; P3 stability is advisory-only and never gates promotion.\n134\t- **Given** a forged definition that is example-stable but unfaithful, **when** autonomous D2 runs, **then** it stamps requires-Phase-F.\n135\t\n136\t## Wave 21 â€” Degradation-tripwire canary (A2 degradation-tripwire â€” global invariant)\n137\t**Deliverables:** the A2(degradation-tripwire) canary: delete the D1/D2 abstain fixtures â‡’ the system STILL refuses to emit green (the 1C runtime promote-gate), as a gated `node --test`.\n138\t**Depends on:** FORMALIZE Lakatosian loop\n139\t**done-when:** with the D1/D2 abstain fixtures deleted, the build still refuses any green/VERIFIED for proof/conceptual claims; the canary fails the build if a green would be emitted.\n140\t- **Given** the abstain fixtures deleted, **when** the degradation-tripwire canary runs, **then** the system still refuses green.\n141\t\n142\t## Wave 22 â€” CONTEXTUALIZE relation-classifier + commission canary (D3)\n143\t**Deliverables:** the native math relation classifier {generalization|specialization|equivalence|instance|structural-analogy}; every connection a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to A3; the commission canary.\n144\t**Depends on:** Degradation-tripwire canary\n145\t**done-when:** each proposed connection is emitted as a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to VERIFY (never settled by analogy); the commission canary holds.\n146\t- **Given** a proposed structural analogy, **when** D3 runs, **then** it is emitted as a CONCEPTUAL claim routed to VERIFY (not settled).\n147\t\n148\t## Wave 23 â€” Autonomous orchestrator + no-dispatch canary (D4)\n149\t**Deliverables:** user-explicit dispatch + an ADVISORY classifier, fail-safe ASK, read-only multi-pillar routing (grows the Wave-14 shim); the A2(no-dispatch) canary, regression-bound to the Wave-14 shim path.\n150\t**Depends on:** CONTEXTUALIZE relation-classifier + commission canary\n151\t**done-when:** the orchestrator routes read-only; the no-dispatch canary proves it cannot settle or commission-dispatch a verdict (no commission-id, no rung-flip) on ANY orchestrator OR Wave-14 shim path.\n152\t- **Given** an attempt by the orchestrator (or the shim) to emit a commission-id or flip a rung, **when** the no-dispatch canary runs, **then** the build fails.\n153\t\n154\t## Wave 24 â€” Gradeable oracle, part A: fixture corpus + red-team set (E1a)\n155\t**Deliverables:** the autonomous-tier fixtures (the iâ€“xiv union: the 6 planted-defect classes Ã— â‰¥3 instances + the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset + the ref-fn-independence fixture + the A4 laundering/recall rosters + the forged-unfaithful-definition fixture + the abstain-payload fixture + a RED-TEAM set incl. forged-artifact, cross-claim replay, same-claim replay, across-restart replay AND crash-mid-mint attempts).\n156\t**Depends on:** Autonomous orchestrator + no-dispatch canary\n157\t**done-when:** the corpus loads, each fixture is labeled with its class + expected verdict, and the red-team forged-artifact / cross-claim / same-claim / across-restart replay / crash-mid-mint attempts are each present and individually asserted as MUST-reject.\n158\t- **Given** the red-team set, **when** E1a's assertions run, **then** the forged-artifact, cross-claim, same-claim, across-restart replay, and crash-mid-mint fixtures are each rejected by the spine.\n159\t\n160\t## Wave 25 â€” Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation (E1b)\n161\t**Deliverables:** the deterministic SCORER computing **Metric G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the **SCORED SUBSET** (the canonical token, used identically here and in DESCRIPTION Â§Residuals: the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and supplies ONLY the false-positive-rate / kâ€² term); the PINNED canned baseline (two stub scorers: always-ABSTAIN AND always-FLAG, scored on the SCORED SUBSET, G computed identically); the ABLATION arm.\n162\t**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part A: fixture corpus + red-team set\n163\t**done-when (cites the pinned constants):** **G(battery-on) > G(better-stub-baseline) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **per-class catch floors met** â€” derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%, convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset**; **ABSTAIN-correctness = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN.\n164\t- **Given** the ablation arm (battery disabled), **when** the scorer runs on the SCORED SUBSET, **then** G drops below battery-on by more than 0.30 (battery is load-bearing).\n165\t- **Given** either stub baseline, **when** the scorer runs, **then** battery-on G exceeds the better stub's G by > 0.30, and all per-class floors + kâ€² + the 100% abstain floor hold (else the wave HALTs).\n166\t\n167\t## Wave 26 â€” Journal integration (E2)\n168\t**Deliverables:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep-loop input feeding the oracle's fixture-failure learning.\n169\t**Depends on:** Gradeable oracle, part B: Metric-G scorer + canned baseline + ablation\n170\t**done-when:** a run appends a 7-field journal entry and the sleep-loop consumes it (tested).\n171\t- **Given** a completed run, **when** journal integration executes, **then** a well-formed 7-field entry is appended and the sleep-loop reads it.\n172\t\n173\t## Wave 27 â€” Author SKILL.md (full) + invocation smoke test (E3) â€” project-DONE\n174\t**Deliverables:** the full tiered-scope SKILL.md headline; the per-pillar usage contract; the explicit Increment-1 acceptance note (\"NS abstain-arms DONE; NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 positive-arm = Increment-2\"); the invocation smoke test; the 5-gate productionization checklist.\n175\t**Depends on:** Journal integration\n176\t**done-when:** an invocation smoke test (a canned input) produces a correctly-stamped abstain/route through the REAL router; the SKILL.md states the Increment-1 acceptance boundary; the 5-gate productionization checklist + manifest checker pass.\n177\t- **Given** a canned proof-bearing input, **when** the skill is invoked end-to-end, **then** it returns a CONJECTURAL+routed result with an honest per-claim rung+verifier-family stamp + advisory payload, and the SKILL.md headline declares NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 as Increment-2.\n178\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8029081b-33f7-47d3-83d8-20728a40fbbf","uuid":"fd3adc3d-5682-4a74-8380-0c684016774d","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:48:27.661Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\ramanujan\\planning\\crucible\\stage2\\handoff\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Ramanujan â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready) â€” v3 (post Stage-2 round 2)\n\ntest-command: node --test test/\n\n**North Star:** Ramanujan = a 6-pillar mathematical-reasoning PARTNER (Understand/Solve/Verify/Dialogue/Formalize/Contextualize) on ONE shared claim-ledger + verify-router spine, governed by THE HONESTY LAW (no same-family-authored object reaches a VERIFIED rung; the autonomous tier settles only literal finite computations bound to a re-executable out-of-model SUBPROCESS artifact; everything else ABSTAINS + routes to an out-of-model certifier). NS1â€“NS9.\n\n## Success criteria (and the Increment-1 acceptance boundary)\nNS1 verified laddered comprehension Â· NS2 generative SOLVE + executable CONTROL Â· NS3 always-on independent VERIFY router by claim type + honest abstain Â· NS4 autoformalization faithfulness Â· NS5 honest per-claim rung+verifier-family stamp Â· NS6 stateful DIALOGUE that never asserts unverified math as settled Â· NS7 interactive FORMALIZE with the human gate Â· NS8 CONTEXTUALIZE composes researchPrime/Gandalf without reimplementing Â· NS9 THE HONESTY LAW (canaries + gradeable oracle).\n\n> **INCREMENT-1 ACCEPTANCE BOUNDARY (explicit).** This is the AUTONOMOUS increment (Phases Aâ€“E). **NS3-routing-lift, NS4-faithfulness, and NS7-human-gate are STRUCTURALLY UNVERIFIABLE here and realized ONLY as their honest abstain+route arm** (ABSTAIN to CONJECTURAL + advisory payload + route to the Increment-2 certifier). Their positive arm is the promotion-gated **Increment-2** (DESCRIPTION.md). Wave-27 project-DONE reads **\"NS abstain-arms DONE; NS3-lift/NS4/NS7 positive-arm = Increment-2\"** â€” NEVER \"NS1â€“9 satisfied\". The only positive VERIFIED lift Increment-1 demonstrates is the A4 literal-computation path (NS9/NS3-computational).\n>\n> Every wave ships real source its new `node --test` tests import and exercise; non-trivial waves carry Given/When/Then. Required-before-build residuals (A0.5a/R1/Metric-G+baseline/S1/S4/P3/P7/P9 + the win32 subprocess & inherited-module contract; P8 = Increment-2) are PINNED in DESCRIPTION.md Â§Residuals with value + owner + terminus-acceptance.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Author SKILL.md skeleton + tiered-scope headline\n**Deliverables:** SKILL.md stub; the tiered-scope headline (\"no autonomous proof verification â€” ACCEPT = computational sub-claim\").\n**Depends on:** â€”\n**done-when:** SKILL.md exists, names all six pillars + the Honesty Law, and the manifest checker passes.\n- **Given** a fresh checkout, **when** the manifest checker runs, **then** it finds SKILL.md naming all six pillars + the Honesty Law and exits 0.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Inheritance presence/interface gate + inherits manifest (A0.5a)\n**Deliverables:** `inherits.manifest.json` (logical-name â†’ resolvable path + expected exports for Phase-0 handoff/journal/sleep, Gandalf v1 commission seam, the three dive engines); a `node --test` gate resolving + version-checking + interface-SHAPE-checking each entry.\n**Depends on:** Author SKILL.md skeleton\n**done-when:** the gate passes green and fails fast (non-zero) on any unresolvable path / version / interface mismatch; AND it round-trips a written counter/spent-nonce value through the inherited durability substrate across a simulated reload (so Wave-4's across-restart replay test cannot pass against an in-memory stub).\n- **Given** a manifest entry with an unresolvable path or changed export shape, **when** the gate runs, **then** it fails fast naming the offending entry.\n- **Given** the inherited durability substrate, **when** the gate writes a counter/spent-nonce value and reloads it across a simulated restart, **then** the value round-trips intact.\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Typed CLAIM ledger + promote() (A1)\n**Deliverables:** the rung ladder REFUTED<UNVERIFIED<CLAIMED<CORROBORATED<OBSERVED; belief-tag = deterministic projection; sticky semantics; `promote()` as the SOLE rung-raiser.\n**Depends on:** Inheritance presence/interface gate + inherits manifest\n**done-when:** the ledger enforces the ladder + sticky semantics and promote() is the only path that raises a rung (tested).\n- **Given** a VERIFIED claim, **when** re-assertion without re-verification occurs, **then** the sticky ledger holds the rung (no flip).\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate (A1.5)\n**Deliverables:** the P9 provenance-binding contract (artifact format + canary out-of-band re-execution/re-hash + a single-use claim-bound nonce that is DURABLE + monotone across restarts via the Phase-0 durability substrate); only the dispatcher writes family-of-record; promote()-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN absent a valid fresh artifact.\n**Depends on:** Typed CLAIM ledger + promote()\n**done-when:** with NO minter present, promote()-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN (NEGATIVE test); a re-presented artifact is rejected for same-claim, cross-claim, AND across-restart replay (the nonce state reloads from the durability substrate); the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE artifact validity, proven by a crash-mid-mint fixture (process death after mint but before durable flush yields NO usable replayable nonce on restart). **Wave-4 positive-path verification is DEFERRED to Wave 9; Wave-4's gate is negative-only.**\n- **Given** a fresh artifact minted+persisted for claim X, **when** the process restarts (state reloaded) and the artifact is re-presented for a second promotion of X, **then** the durable single-use nonce rejects it.\n- **Given** a process death AFTER mint but BEFORE the durable counter flush, **when** the process restarts, **then** no usable replayable nonce exists (persist is ordered-before validity).\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Inheritance conformance gate (A0.5b)\n**Deliverables:** a `node --test` gate exercising each inherited seam against the real A1 ledger / A3 router contract, with pinned per-seam contract assertions.\n**Depends on:** Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate\n**done-when:** each inherited seam passes its conformance fixture; a planted non-conforming seam fails the gate non-zero naming the seam; gates Phase B+.\n- **Given** an inherited seam violating the A1/A3 contract, **when** the conformance gate runs, **then** it fails non-zero naming the seam.\n\n## Wave 6 â€” Honesty-Law canary suite, core (A2-core)\n**Deliverables:** (1) independence; (2) inverted-completeness; (3) transitions-invariant; (4) flip-law â€” all verifying the re-executed artifact (proposeâ‰ adjudicate).\n**Depends on:** Out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate\n**done-when:** all four canaries are green and each FAILS the build on its planted violation.\n- **Given** a same-family object asserting VERIFIED with a self-authored stamp, **when** independence + flip-law run, **then** the build fails.\n\n## Wave 7 â€” VERIFY router skeleton (A3)\n**Deliverables:** typed-claim DECOMPOSE â†’ DISPATCH â†’ route to the strongest APPLICABLE generator-independent verifier â†’ honest ABSTAIN/FLAG + advisory payload; the FLIP LAW; per-claim rung + artifact-backed verifier-family STAMP + advisory NOTES.\n**Depends on:** Honesty-Law canary suite, core\n**done-when:** any decomposed claim routes to an applicable verifier or ABSTAINS+routes with an advisory payload; no silent pass (tested).\n- **Given** a proof-bearing claim with no autonomous verifier, **when** the router runs, **then** it ABSTAINS to CONJECTURAL, routes out-of-model, and emits an advisory payload.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” Autonomous-VERIFIED gate, part A: default-deny grammar + laundering battery (A4a)\n**Deliverables:** the literal-execution recognizer as a CLOSED default-deny whitelist GRAMMAR over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; bigint/rational, NO float; NO symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); anything unparsed/outside â‡’ ABSTAIN+route; the P7 laundering battery incl. deep-nested-smuggle cases.\n**Depends on:** VERIFY router skeleton\n**done-when:** the grammar rejects (ABSTAIN+route) 100% of the laundering battery including a composition that smuggles an out-of-grammar node anywhere in the tree; it raises no VERIFIED rung (no minter).\n- **Given** a smuggled non-literal input (incl. an out-of-grammar node nested in an otherwise-valid tree), **when** A4a runs, **then** it ABSTAINS+routes.\n\n## Wave 9 â€” Autonomous-VERIFIED gate, part B: firewall subprocess + artifact-mint + recall roster (A4b)\n**Deliverables:** the firewall as an OUT-OF-MODEL execution SUBPROCESS (child `node`, no shell, per-claim hermetic temp-dir, EXACT-arithmetic evaluation) producing the re-executable Wave-4 artifact with a recorded runtime fingerprint (node major + canonicalization version); wiring to the Wave-4 canary positive path; the P7 positive-recall roster incl. nested-composition case