n## Wave 12 â€” Coverage-stamp canary (B2b â€” A2 coverage-stamp)\n**Deliverables:** the A2 coverage-stamp canary (predicate_domain âŠ‡ claim_domain from the execution trace; caps at CLAIMED on warranty_excludes[]â‰ âˆ… / anchor_coverage<full), as a gated `node --test`.\n**Depends on:** Firewall builder + anchors + stamps + S4 invariant\n**done-when:** the coverage-stamp canary fails the build on an over-trusted reduced-warranty pass.\n- **Given** a firewall with warranty_excludes[] non-empty, **when** the coverage-stamp canary runs, **then** a VERIFIED rung is refused (capped at CLAIMED).\n\n## Wave 13 â€” Commission emitters + no-inline boundary canary (B3)\n**Deliverables:** typed Gandalf + researchPrime commission-envelope EMITTERS; the no-inline-reimplementation boundary canary (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n**Depends on:** Coverage-stamp canary\n**done-when:** envelopes emit (never dispatch) and the boundary canary fails the build on an inline reimplementation.\n- **Given** an inline researchPrime/Gandalf reimplementation, **when** the boundary canary runs, **then** the build fails (import-graph + forbidden-symbol).\n\n## Wave 14 â€” M1 read-only dispatch shim (B-shim) â€” closes Milestone M1 (comprehension-only preview)\n**Deliverables:** a minimal read-only single-pillar dispatch shim.\n**Depends on:** Commission emitters + no-inline boundary canary\n**done-when:** the shim routes a user request to UNDERSTAND read-only and satisfies the EXACT predicate the Wave-23 no-dispatch canary will later assert: **no commission-id emitted AND no rung-flip on any shim path** (wave-local check; regression-bound by Wave 23).\n- **Given** any shim path, **when** Wave-14's check runs, **then** no commission-id is emitted and no rung is flipped.\n\n## Wave 15 â€” Generation + typed-claim decompose (C1)\n**Deliverables:** a stateless Polya/Schoenfeld GENERATION pass â†’ typed-claim DECOMPOSE into the A1 ledger.\n**Depends on:** M1 read-only dispatch shim\n**done-when:** a new problem yields a candidate decomposed into typed claims, all at UNVERIFIED, in the ledger.\n- **Given** a new problem, **when** C1 runs, **then** every emitted claim is at UNVERIFIED until the router verifies it.\n\n## Wave 16 â€” Claim-type dispatch classifier (C2)\n**Deliverables:** a fail-safe, separate-pass claim-type DISPATCH classifier with conservative escalation to the proof route.\n**Depends on:** Generation + typed-claim decompose\n**done-when:** ambiguous/borderline claims escalate conservatively to the proof route (ABSTAIN+route), never silently to autonomous-VERIFIED (tested).\n- **Given** a borderline claim, **when** C2 runs, **then** it routes to the proof route (ABSTAIN), never to autonomous-VERIFIED.\n\n## Wave 17 â€” Metacognitive CONTROL state machine + ABANDON fixture (C3)\n**Deliverables:** the CONTROL state machine; the S1 thresholds + gap-function (budget=8; switch=no progress in last 3; ABANDON=2 consecutive switches); graded over a pinned progress-boolean stream.\n**Depends on:** Claim-type dispatch classifier\n**done-when:** on the pinned canned non-converging fixture the machine ABANDONs via the GAP-FUNCTION strictly before step 8 (reason=gap-function, not budget-exhausted), leaving the claim UNVERIFIED/CONJECTURAL.\n- **Given** the pinned non-converging fixture, **when** CONTROL runs, **then** it ABANDONs with reason=gap-function before step 8.\n\n## Wave 18 â€” In-process adversarial advisory layer (C4)\n**Deliverables:** the in-process Gandalf/researchPrime critique + faithfulness-restatement discipline, writing the NOTES field ONLY.\n**Depends on:** Metacognitive CONTROL state machine + ABANDON fixture\n**done-when:** advisory critique writes NOTES and can never change a rung (tested).\n- **Given** an advisory critique, **when** C4 runs, **then** the NOTES field updates but the rung is unchanged.\n\n## Wave 19 â€” DIALOGUE state machine (D1)\n**Deliverables:** the Lakatos loop; mixed-initiative; the structured emission contract; 